STEPS={10:'',11:'MEASURE',12:'TRACE',13:'TEST',14:'RECOVER',15:'COMPARE',16:'CONTRACT',17:'FAILURE',20:'INTEGRATE'}
EXAMPLES={
10:('“Add another server; the system is reliable.”','A second independently powered server can reduce a single-server outage. It does not remove a shared requirements error. Check failover under the relevant load before relying on it.'),
11:('“The test passed, so reliability is guaranteed.”','In a different example, 2 failures in 1,000 transactions gives 0.002 failures per transaction. This estimates the observed sample under its profile; it is not a confidence bound or a guarantee about production.'),
12:('“The barrier is safe because tests passed.”','For a different machine, a trapped-hand hazard is linked to an interlock requirement and a proposed obstruction test. A passing daylight test would not establish behavior with the sensor disconnected.'),
13:('“The page hides the record, so authorization works.”','For a different booking record, user A requests user B’s identifier directly from the API. The proposed test expects denial and no protected content; it records the actor, object and inspected response.'),
14:('“The backup restarts, so the service recovers.”','For a different help desk, recovery requires an authorized operator to retrieve the current task list, record new work, and reconcile it after restoration. A server restart alone does not test that sequence.'),
15:('“Choose the product with more features.”','For a different configurable package, required lifetime exceeds documented support. Record that mismatch and the exit-data unknown; compare a bounded evaluation with the alternative rather than inventing costs.'),
16:('“The names and types match, so integration is correct.”','For a different temperature adapter, matching numeric types does not establish Celsius/Fahrenheit semantics. State the conversion and an expected boundary result, then report the actual result separately.'),
17:('“Retry until it works; duplicates cannot happen.”','For a different message service, the first action may commit before its acknowledgment is lost. A repeated identity and durable outcome record can prevent a second modeled effect; external effects need separate evidence.'),
20:('“Every API passes, so the shared service is ready.”','For a different city dashboard, acceptance includes timestamps, feed loss and independent version changes. The coordinator records what each owner agreed to and what remains useful without one feed.')}
def lab_markup(n):
 if n==16:
  instructions='Write at least three cases: a valid duration, the 120-minute upper boundary, and an invalid input. Each case is a JSON object with name, durationMinutes, expectedStatus (accepted or rejected), and expectedSeconds (a number for accepted input, null for rejected input). Include an expected result before running. The component accepts 1–7200 seconds; the adapter input is minutes.'
  code='// Baseline adapter forwards minutes unchanged.\nseconds = durationMinutes;\n// Corrected adapter converts minutes to seconds.\nseconds = durationMinutes * 60;\n// Both models reject nonnumeric/nonfinite input or seconds outside [1, 7200].\n// An accepted call stores seconds. Room conflicts and concurrency are outside this model.'
  shape='[{"name":"my case","durationMinutes":YOUR_INPUT,"expectedStatus":"accepted or rejected","expectedSeconds":YOUR_EXPECTATION}]'
 else:
  instructions='Write at least two cases. Include a restart with a repeated request identity, and a case containing a genuinely different identity. Each case is a JSON object with name, events (an ordered array), and expectedReservations. Allowed events: send:ID, retry:ID, lose-response, restart. Start with send:ID. Every request event executes; lose-response discards only its response. Predict the final reservation count before running.'
  code='// Requests are processed sequentially in one teaching booking store.\n// Baseline: deduplication records live in service memory; restart clears them.\n// Corrected: request identity and outcome are persisted atomically with the reservation.\n// Same identity returns the recorded outcome; a new identity creates a new reservation.\n// Response loss never rolls back a committed reservation.\n// No real network, concurrency, payment service or deployed database is exercised.'
  shape='[{"name":"my case","events":["send:YOUR_ID","lose-response","restart","retry:YOUR_ID"],"expectedReservations":YOUR_EXPECTATION}]'
 return f'''<section class="card" id="practical"><p class="ey">SMALL EXECUTABLE LAB · PART OF THE EXISTING ARTIFACT</p><h2>{'Contract tests' if n==16 else 'Retry and restart tests'}</h2><p>{instructions}</p><p>Budget 15–20 minutes within the assignment. The run log replaces a paragraph describing hypothetical execution. Keep your actual failures; explain any wrong prediction. Passing tests is not an automatic grade.</p><details><summary>Inspect the teaching-model rules</summary><pre style="white-space:pre-wrap">{esc(code)}</pre></details><label for="labPrediction" class="field-label">Predict what each model will do and why.</label><textarea id="labPrediction" placeholder="My expected difference, and the concept that explains it…"></textarea><label for="labCases" class="field-label">Write your executable test cases as JSON.</label><p class="hint">Replace the uppercase placeholders; they are a schema illustration, not runnable answers.</p><textarea id="labCases" spellcheck="false" placeholder="{esc(shape)}" style="font:16px/1.5 monospace;min-height:200px"></textarea><div class="buttons"><button type="button" data-lab-mode="baseline">Run baseline model</button><button type="button" data-lab-mode="corrected">Run corrected model</button></div><p id="labStatus" role="status" aria-live="polite">Both runs are required; this is an offline teaching model.</p><pre id="labOutput" style="white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:16px/1.5 monospace"></pre><label for="labEvidence" class="field-label">Local execution record · included in export</label><textarea id="labEvidence" readonly style="min-height:140px" placeholder="Generated after a local run. Changing the test cases clears this record."></textarea></section>'''

